hi there Steve Kaufman here to talk  about language learning  remember if you enjoy these videos  please subscribe today I want to talk  about what I consider to be the most  important language skill and that is  comprehension all right now there are  language measurements of success or of  level and I've often said that your  vocabulary and primarily your passive  vocabulary is the best indicator of your  level at least of your potential level  because you need words all right but in  terms of a skill to me comprehension is  the most important and I'm going to  explain why using a number of different  examples this came to me actually while  I was watching a movie it was on TV it  was a Danish Swedish cooperative  production and people are speaking  Swedish and Danish  but they understand each other and  sometimes the Dane has to slow down a  little bit because Danish is harder for  the Swedes to understand than vice-versa  and I started thinking you know there  are a number of these kinds of  situations where people will speak two  different languages and communicate very  effectively Ukraine is a perfect example  many people there are quite bilingual  speak Russian and Ukrainian some people  don't speak Ukrainian but they  understand Ukrainian perfectly well so  it's not uncommon to see people speaking  and one person speaks Ukrainian the  other speaks Russian and they're both  communicating it's always been somewhat  strange to me for example that there are  ministers of the Ukrainian government  who never speak Ukrainian but they  understand it and there are certain  politicians who will be interviewed on  Ukrainian television and the questioner  speaks Ukrainian and the answer comes  back in Russian there's not a problem so  I think of other similar language pairs  you know like Spanish and Portuguese  when I was working on my Portuguese I  was listening to certain Portuguese  podcasts from Portugal and if they have  a span  the Spaniard just speaks Spanish and the  audience who are from Portugal will  understand him it doesn't go quite as  easily the other way but the point is  that there are situations and I would  imagine the same is true insofar as  Arabic is concerned I don't know Arabic  but I gather that at some level they  understand each other or they don't I  don't know but but if they were if for  example if I were to go to Denmark I  would have trouble understanding if I  were to focus and because we now have  Danish at link I would spend you know a  few weeks listening to content looking  up the words get myself familiar to the  sound of Danish I could go to Denmark  understand everything that was said and  speak to them as Swedish and I wouldn't  have a problem  similarly throughout Latin America if  Spanish speakers were to put a little  effort into developing the ability to  understand Portuguese again granted the  Brazilian Portuguese is easier to  understand than the Portuguese from  Portugal but very quickly they could go  to Brazil and if people in Brazil spent  a little put a little effort into  understanding Spanish then they could  communicate using two languages so at  least at that level comprehension is  enough for people to achieve  communication because the languages  themselves are so similar you could say  the same about Mandarin and Cantonese I  was at a reception the other evening and  there was a student there from China who  had been living in Vancouver and she  said all Cantonese is so difficult to  learn is more difficult than French yeah  not true at all  if a Mandarin speaker wants to be able  to understand Cantonese the vocabulary  is 95% the same it doesn't take much  effort of course in all of these  situations there is this element of the  will do you really want to understand it  a lot of Cantonese speakers who don't  speak Mandarin very well understand  Mandarin so this is just talking about  community  between these sort of similar pairs of  languages now if we are learning a  language that's not similar for example  I'm learning Greek right now and my goal  with Greek is to understand because I  can say simple things in Greek I can  have simple conversations in Greek  that's not difficult because it's a  controlled environment I talk about  things that I am familiar with that you  know I use a limited range of vocabulary  which means that the person I'm talking  to my high talkie tooter is using a  limited range of vocabulary but now I  found these wonderful podcasts on the  Parthenon and on Greek history and and  I'm having them transcribed but I I want  to get to where I can understand these  because once you achieve a high level of  comprehension then your ability to speak  can quickly come up as long as you have  the right attitude and then when I go to  Crete I will be prepared I'll have a  large vocabulary I'll have good  comprehension and even if I struggle to  speak at first I'll be able to stay in  the game comprehension which requires  vocabulary comprehension is the sort of  number one defense you can cope know  what no matter what is thrown at you you  understand you can then slowly you know  find ways to express what it is you want  to say now having said all of that and  saying that comprehension is the  fundamental skill we should work on  comprehension work on doing a lot of  listening and reading work on our  vocabulary and then there are people to  say well I understand very well but I  can't speak when I go to speak I can't  find the words of course that's true and  ultimately you have to speak a lot and  in order to speak a lot you have to be  prepared to put yourself into situations  where you have trouble speaking where  you sound foolish where you feel you  don't have enough time to say what you  want to say because there are four or  five people speaking and in this  language  you understand more or less what they're  saying and you want to say something and  then all of a sudden you think you don't  have enough time when there's pressure  on you or you think you did poorly of  course all of that is there and you have  to be willing to put yourself through  that you have to be willing to sound  less than intelligent be willing to  expose yourself to that kind of an  uncomfortable feeling however if you  don't have comprehension if you don't  understand what people are saying if you  don't have the ability through good  comprehension to enjoy books to enjoy  radio programs to enjoy movies all of  these things which are going to increase  the level of your language and things  that you can do on your own if you don't  have that comprehension level then the  your speaking level will never improve  so the fundamental skill is  comprehension how far you take that in  terms of being able to use what might  appear to some to be a passive level of  knowledge how far you take that into  your speaking is entirely a matter of  your own attitude if you are prepared to  expose yourself to that the  uncomfortable feeling of knowing that  you're struggling knowing that you're  making mistakes knowing that you haven't  got enough time to say what you want to  say knowing that there are words there  that you know that you can't find when  you need to use them all of these  uncomfortable feelings are on an are an  absolutely integral part of language  learning so that part of it you have to  decide for yourself but as a strategy  when I learn languages and that's  certainly the case right now with my  agree I am focusing on improving my  level of comprehension and it is slowly  improving just through the massive  exposure that I'm getting through my  listening and reading and of course  working on link so that's why I think  comprehension you know what I should  well I'll do the next video I will do in  a mixture of these paired languages  Spanish Portuguese Ukrainian Russian and  so forth just for the fun of it  okay bye for now  [Music]
 

